---
// Paper Table 4: median Limitations-section length and average number of
// distinct limitation codes per section, by conference and year. Static, zero JS.
import { SECTION_EVOLUTION } from "../../data/resultsData";

const years = SECTION_EVOLUTION.acl.map((r) => r.year);
const rows = years.map((year) => ({
  year,
  acl: SECTION_EVOLUTION.acl.find((r) => r.year === year)!,
  emnlp: SECTION_EVOLUTION.emnlp.find((r) => r.year === year)!,
}));
---
<figure class="data-figure section-length">
  <figcaption>
    <span class="paper-ref">Table 4 in the paper</span>
    Median length of the Limitations section (words) and the average number of distinct limitation codes per section.
  </figcaption>
  <div class="data-table-wrap">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th rowspan="2">Year</th>
          <th colspan="2" class="num group">ACL</th>
          <th colspan="2" class="num group">EMNLP</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th class="num">Median words</th>
          <th class="num">Codes / section</th>
          <th class="num">Median words</th>
          <th class="num">Codes / section</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{r.year}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.acl.medWords.toFixed(1)}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.acl.codesPerPaper.toFixed(2)}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.emnlp.medWords.toFixed(1)}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.emnlp.codesPerPaper.toFixed(2)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</figure>

<aside class="observation" aria-label="Observation">
  <span class="observation-label">Observation</span>
  <p>
    The paper reads this as authors adopting a more concise, multifaceted approach: fitting more kinds of limitation
    into roughly the same space rather than describing a few in detail. One possible implication is that each
    limitation now gets less elaboration, with sections leaning toward brief mentions rather than in-depth discussion.
  </p>
  <p class="observation-caveat">
    This is an observation, not a finding: the data count words and codes, not how thoroughly each limitation is
    explained, so confirming it would need a closer reading of the sections themselves.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .section-length {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .observation {
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
    max-width: 860px;
  }
  .observation-label {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.05rem 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--card);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .observation p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .observation .observation-caveat {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
</style>
